  ('lemon-grass', 'croptype-943756684079', 'spices-condiments-medicinal-aromatic', 'Lemon grass', '{"am": "ሎሚ ሳር"}'::jsonb, 'Cymbopogon citratus (DC) Stapf', 'WGARC', 'http://196.191.93.34/moa-portal/cropopen/varieites/crops/Lemon grass.jpg', NULL, 3, 'ACTIVE'),
  ('lemon-scented-eucalyptus', 'croptype-402091607078', 'spices-condiments-medicinal-aromatic', 'Lemon scented eucalyptus', '{"am": "ሽቶ ባሕርዛፍ"}'::jsonb, 'Eucalyptus citriodora', 'WGARC', 'http://196.191.93.34/moa-portal/cropopen/varieites/crops/Lemon scented eucalyptus.jpg', NULL, 1, 'ACTIVE'),
  ('lemon-verbena', 'croptype-225922814390', 'spices-condiments-medicinal-aromatic', 'Lemon verbena', '{"am": "ሎሚናት"}'::jsonb, 'Aloysia triphylla L.', 'WGARC', 'http://196.191.93.34/moa-portal/cropopen/varieites/crops/Lemon verbena.jpg', NULL, 1, 'ACTIVE'),
  ('lentil', 'croptype-606234725254', 'food-legume', 'Lentil', '{"am": "ምስር"}'::jsonb, 'Lens culinaris', 'DZARC', 'http://196.191.93.34/moa-portal/cropopen/varieites/crops/Lentil.jpg', 'Lentil is one of the highland crops widely grown in Ethiopia. It is largely produced in the highland & semi-highland regions of the county mainly on clay soil. During 2020/21 cropping season, 84,511.63 hectares of land is covered with Lentil and about 1,130,178.82 quintals were produced. This crop is widely used for food because of its high protein content. Apart from this, due to its ability to fix nitrogen, it is used in crop rotation with the nationally important crops. Although the above mentioned realities indicate the national importance of lentil, the national yield is only about 8.35 quintals per hectare.

The lentil is a much-branched annual, up to 18 inches high, with slender, angular stems. Its leaves are pinnate, with 4-7 pairs of more or less oval leaflets, about 1/2 inches long. The small white flowers are papilionaceous with a large upper peta, two lateral petals, and two narrow petals between these.', 15, 'ACTIVE'),
  ('lettuce', 'croptype-523478583483', 'fruit-and-vegetables', 'Lettuce', NULL, 'Lactuca sativa', 'HARC', 'http://196.191.93.34/moa-portal/cropopen/varieites/crops/lettuce.jpg', NULL, 15, 'ACTIVE'),
  ('lima-bean-butter-bean', 'croptype-474245217289', 'food-legume', 'Lima bean (butter bean)', NULL, 'Phaseolus lunatus', 'Melkassa Agricultural Research Cent', 'http://196.191.93.34/moa-portal/cropopen/varieites/crops/limabean.jpg', 'LIma bean (Phaseolus lunatus L.) is a species of beans which originated from the regions of Central America and Andes Mountains. The crop has distinctive features that include different types of pods, seed size, shape, thickness, color and growth forms. The crop is readily distinguished from other species in that it possesses fine ridges in the seed coat that radiate from the "eye". The pods are wide, flat, and slightly curved. The plant grows as a perennial in the tropics and is normally cultivated as an annual crop. It requires a longer season and warmer weather than most varieties of common bean (Phaseoulus vulgaris). It can grow within annual temperature 0f 16-27oC and annual ran fall 900-2000mm. The crop has deep rooted, drought tolerant and wide environmental adpatation character. It has numerous uses like animal feed, soil improvement, human food (immature and dry seeds) and medicine.', 2, 'ACTIVE'),
  ('linseed', 'croptype-551131664280', 'oil-seeds', 'Linseed', '{"am": "ተልባ"}'::jsonb, 'Linum usitatissimum L.', 'HARC', 'http://196.191.93.34/moa-portal/cropopen/varieites/crops/Linseed.jpg', 'In Ethiopia the seed is commonly roasted, ground and mixed with spices and some water to be served along with local breads. It is also consumed in soups, soft drinks and with porridges or cooked potatoes. Its industrial use is higher tan all other oil crops. Its highest contribution in paint, soap, lubricant and pharmaceutical factories helped to gain international attention. In the 2020/21 cropping season, 78,921.37 ha of land was covered with linseed and the production was estimated to be 804,566.42.', 22, 'ACTIVE'),
  ('maize', 'croptype-592280314975', 'cereal', 'Maize', '{"am": "በቆሎ"}'::jsonb, 'Zea mays L.', 'BKARC', 'http://196.191.93.34/moa-portal/cropopen/varieites/crops/Maize.jpg', NULL, 85, 'ACTIVE'),
  ('majoram-oregano', 'croptype-131068677144', 'spices-condiments-medicinal-aromatic', 'Majoram/ Oregano', NULL, 'Origannum vulgaris L.', 'WGARC', 'http://196.191.93.34/moa-portal/cropopen/varieites/crops/Majoram.jpg', NULL, 1, 'ACTIVE'),
  ('mango', 'croptype-899576185560', 'fruit-and-vegetables', 'Mango', '{"am": "ማንጎ"}'::jsonb, 'Mangifera indica L.', 'MARC', 'http://196.191.93.34/moa-portal/cropopen/varieites/crops/Mango.jpg', NULL, 4, 'ACTIVE'),
  ('mung-bean', 'croptype-446541774435', 'food-legume', 'Mung bean', '{"am": "ማሾ"}'::jsonb, 'Vigna radiata L.', 'MARC', 'http://196.191.93.34/moa-portal/cropopen/varieites/crops/Mung bean.jpg', 'Mung bean is in the legume family of plants and is closely related to adzuki and cowpea. It is a warm season annual, highly branched and having trifoliate leaves like the other legumes. Both upright and vine types of growth habit occur in mung bean, with plants varying from one to five feet in length. The pale yellow flowers are borne in clusters of 12-15 near the top of the plant. Mature pods are variable in color (yellowish-brown to black), about five inches long, and contain 10 to 15 seeds', 4, 'ACTIVE'),
  ('musk-melon', 'croptype-483386148392', 'fruit-and-vegetables', 'Musk melon', NULL, 'Cucumis melo', 'MARC', 'http://196.191.93.34/moa-portal/cropopen/varieites/crops/muskmelon.jpg', NULL, 2, 'ACTIVE'),
  ('noug', 'croptype-251134569325', 'oil-seeds', 'Noug', '{"am": "ኑግ"}'::jsonb, 'Guizotia abyssinica L.', 'HARC', 'http://196.191.93.34/moa-portal/cropopen/varieites/crops/Noug.jpg', 'Noug is an oil seed crop, indigenous to Ethiopia and holds significant promise for improving rural livelihoods in Sub Saharan Africa. The species is used in intercropping systems, grows on poor but also extremely wet soils, and contributes to soil conservation. It contributes up to 50% of the Ethiopian oil-seed crop. Noug diversity is numerous in Ethiopia and Eritrea and local farmers are able to distinguish many landraces. Apart from Africa (East and South African countries), noug is cultivated in parts of South Asia, where it was introduced thousand years ago, and the West Indies.

Noug belongs to the Compositae family and is closely related to sunflower. It differs from domesticated sunflower mainly due to its high level of branching, numerous flower heads and small seeds. The oil content of noug seed varies from 30 to 50%. The fatty acid composition is typical for seed oils of the Compositae family with linoleic acid being the dominant components.

It is one of the major oil crops of Ethiopia with the highest share of area coverage. The oil quality is very high and is comparable to the cooking oils used in the developed countries. In 2020/21 cropping season, 191,766.00 ha of land was covered with noug and about 2,147,979.02 quintals were estimated to be produced.', 5, 'ACTIVE'),
  ('okra', 'croptype-253966230443', 'fruit-and-vegetables', 'Okra', NULL, 'Abelmoschus esculentus L. Monech', NULL, 'http://196.191.93.34/moa-portal/cropopen/varieites/crops/okra.jpg', NULL, 5, 'ACTIVE'),
  ('onion', 'croptype-957663023880', 'fruit-and-vegetables', 'Onion', '{"am": "ሽንኩርት"}'::jsonb, 'Allium cepa L.', 'MARC', 'http://196.191.93.34/moa-portal/cropopen/varieites/crops/onion.jpg', 'Onion is one of the bulb crops belonging to the family Alliaceae. It is an important bulb crop in Ethiopia. It is considerably important in the daily Ethiopian diet. All plant parts are edible, but the bulbs and the lower stem sections are the most popular as seasonings or as vegetables in stews.

Onion contributes substantially to the national economy, adapt from overcoming local demands. Products like bulbs and cut flowers are exported to different countries of the world. With the growing irrigated agriculture in the country, there is great potential for extensive onion seed and dry bulb production in the different production belts of the country. Onion prefers well-drained sandy loam with a high content of organic matter. The optimum altitude range for Onion production is between 700 and 2200 masl. and the optimum growing temperature lies between 15oC and 23oC.
During 2020/21 Meher cropping season, the total area under production reaches over 38,952.58 hectares and the production is estimated to be over 3,460,480.88 quintals.', 32, 'ACTIVE'),
  ('pakchoi', 'croptype-807023033164', 'fruit-and-vegetables', 'Pakchoi', NULL, 'Brassica Rapa var. chinensis', 'MARC', 'http://196.191.93.34/moa-portal/cropopen/varieites/crops/packchoi.jfif', NULL, 2, 'ACTIVE'),
  ('palmarosa', 'croptype-308506276670', 'spices-condiments-medicinal-aromatic', 'Palmarosa', '{"am": "ጠጅ ሳር"}'::jsonb, 'Cymbopogon martinii L.', 'WGARC', 'http://196.191.93.34/moa-portal/cropopen/varieites/crops/Palmarosa.jpg', NULL, 2, 'ACTIVE'),
  ('papaya', 'croptype-446477758334', 'fruit-and-vegetables', 'Papaya', '{"am": "ፓፓያ"}'::jsonb, 'Carica papaya L.', 'MARC', 'http://196.191.93.34/moa-portal/cropopen/varieites/crops/papaya.avif', NULL, 3, 'ACTIVE'),
  ('peach', 'croptype-365988738387', 'fruit-and-vegetables', 'Peach', '{"am": "ኮክ"}'::jsonb, 'Prunus persica', 'HARC', 'http://196.191.93.34/moa-portal/cropopen/varieites/crops/Peach.jpg', NULL, 2, 'ACTIVE'),
  ('pearl-millet', 'croptype-809346300724', 'cereal', 'Pearl millet', NULL, 'Pennisetum glaucum L.R.Br', 'MARC', 'http://196.191.93.34/moa-portal/cropopen/varieites/crops/pearl_millet.webp', 'Pearl millet is the most widely grown type of millet. Grown in Africa and the Indian subcontinent since prehistoric times, it is generally accepted that pearl millet originated in Africa and was subsequently introduced into India. Its origin has been traced to tropical Africa. The center center of diversity for the crop is in the Sahel zone of West Africa. Cultivation subsequently spread to east and southern Africa, and southern Asia.

Pearl millet is a new crop for Ethiopian farmers both in terms of cultivation and utilization, indicating the urgent needed for further study. Millet being a highly cross-pollinated crop, maintenance of seed-purity is a challenge that needs higher attention. The seeds of millet ripen first in the upper part of the head and then successively downward.', 1, 'ACTIVE'),
  ('pepper', 'croptype-254997560878', 'fruit-and-vegetables', 'Pepper', '{"am": "ቃሪያ"}'::jsonb, 'Capsicum frutescence', 'MARC', 'http://196.191.93.34/moa-portal/cropopen/varieites/crops/Chili-Pepper-800x416.jpg', NULL, 37, 'ACTIVE'),
  ('peppermint', 'croptype-320693250669', 'spices-condiments-medicinal-aromatic', 'Peppermint', '{"am": "ናና"}'::jsonb, 'Mentha piperita L.', 'WGARC', 'http://196.191.93.34/moa-portal/cropopen/varieites/crops/Peppermint.jpg', NULL, 1, 'ACTIVE'),
  ('pineapple', 'croptype-872170508253', 'fruit-and-vegetables', 'Pineapple', '{"am": "አናናስ"}'::jsonb, 'Ananas comosus', 'JARC', 'http://196.191.93.34/moa-portal/cropopen/varieites/crops/Pineapple.jpg', NULL, 2, 'ACTIVE'),
  ('potato', 'croptype-711524051980', 'roots-and-tubers', 'Potato', '{"am": "ድንች"}'::jsonb, 'Solanum tubersum', 'HARC', 'http://196.191.93.34/moa-portal/cropopen/varieites/crops/irishPotato.jpg', 'In volume of production potato ranks fourth in the world after maize, rice and wheat. Among root crops, potato ranks first in volume produced and consumed, followed by cassava, sweeet potato, and yam.', 39, 'ACTIVE'),
  ('pyrethrum', 'croptype-392924463876', 'spices-condiments-medicinal-aromatic', 'Pyrethrum', '{"am": "ፓይረትረም"}'::jsonb, 'Chrysanthemum cinerariaefolium', 'WGARC', 'http://196.191.93.34/moa-portal/cropopen/varieites/crops/Pyrethrum.jpg', NULL, 2, 'ACTIVE'),
  ('quinoa', 'croptype-903755949559', 'cereal', 'Quinoa', '{"am": "ኪዩና"}'::jsonb, 'Chenopodium quinoa Willd', 'MARC', 'http://196.191.93.34/moa-portal/cropopen/varieites/crops/Quinoa.jpg', 'Will be updated', 1, 'ACTIVE'),
  ('rapeseed', 'croptype-851624380964', 'oil-seeds', 'Rapeseed', NULL, 'Brassica napus', 'HARC', 'http://196.191.93.34/moa-portal/cropopen/varieites/crops/Rapeseed.jpg', 'Different research data show that the crop has about 40-46% oil content. Even though the crop is widely produced in the coutnry, its high "erucic" and "linoleic" acids content has limited its use either for food or feed. In 2020/21 cropping season, 7,917.47 ha of land are covered with Brassica spp. and the annual production was estimated at 125,757.89 quintals.', 4, 'ACTIVE'),
  ('red-beet', 'croptype-380387057571', 'roots-and-tubers', 'Red beet', NULL, 'Beta vulgaris', 'HawARC', 'http://196.191.93.34/moa-portal/cropopen/varieites/crops/red beet.jpg', NULL, 1, 'ACTIVE'),
  ('rice', 'croptype-383064785940', 'cereal', 'Rice', '{"am": "ሩዝ"}'::jsonb, 'Oryza sativa L. or Oryza glaberrima', 'FNRTC', 'http://196.191.93.34/moa-portal/cropopen/varieites/crops/Rice.jpg', NULL, 40, 'ACTIVE'),
  ('rose', 'croptype-118917784167', 'spices-condiments-medicinal-aromatic', 'Rose', '{"am": "ጽጌረዳ"}'::jsonb, 'Rosa damascena Mill', 'WGARC', 'http://196.191.93.34/moa-portal/cropopen/varieites/crops/Rosa_damascena.JPG', NULL, 1, 'ACTIVE'),
  ('rosemary', 'croptype-598990689109', 'spices-condiments-medicinal-aromatic', 'Rosemary', '{"am": "ጥብስ ቅጠል"}'::jsonb, 'Rosmarinus officinalis', 'WGARC', 'http://196.191.93.34/moa-portal/cropopen/varieites/crops/Rosemary.jpg', NULL, 3, 'ACTIVE'),
  ('safflower', 'croptype-784104217122', 'oil-seeds', 'Safflower', '{"am": "ሱፍ"}'::jsonb, 'Carthamus tinctorius L.', 'HARC', 'http://196.191.93.34/moa-portal/cropopen/varieites/crops/Safflower.jpg', 'Safflower is an annual composite plant from the asteraceae family. This herb is highly branched with many long sharp spines on the leaves. Plants are generally 30-50 cm tall with globular flower heads (capitula) and commonly, brilliant yellow, orange or red flowers. It is widely grown for its red or orange flower heads and seeds that yield valuable oil. Safflower seed oil is flavorless and colorless, and nutritionally similar to sunflower oil. It is used mainly in cosmetics and as cooking oil, in salad dressing, and for the production of margarine.', 2, 'ACTIVE'),
  ('sage', 'croptype-146185367281', 'spices-condiments-medicinal-aromatic', 'Sage', NULL, 'Saliva officinalis L.', 'WGARC', 'http://196.191.93.34/moa-portal/cropopen/varieites/crops/Sage.jpg', NULL, 1, 'ACTIVE'),
  ('sesame', 'croptype-174776413012', 'oil-seeds', 'Sesame', '{"am": "ሰሊጥ"}'::jsonb, 'Sesamum indicum', 'HuARC', 'http://196.191.93.34/moa-portal/cropopen/varieites/crops/Sesame.jpg', 'It is an annual short-day warm season plant and mostly grown as a rain fed crop in the rainy season in the semi-arid regions of the tropics and subtropics. In Ethiopia, sesame seed grows mainly in the Northern and Northwestern region. The sowing is done during June to mid September and harvesting is from October onwards. The country is one of the major sesame exporting nations, currently ranked at the fourth position in world markets. Types of Sesame Seed in Ethiopia are Humera, Gondar and Wollega types where Humera Sesame seed is the main type exported by the country. Sesame is used for food. The dried seeds are eaten in soups and, mixed with sugar, are a popular sweet in Africa and Asia. It is used as a salad and cooking oil. The oil is also used in the manufacture of margarine and compound cooking fats.', 33, 'ACTIVE'),
  ('shallot', 'croptype-278506332520', 'fruit-and-vegetables', 'Shallot', '{"am": "ሽንኩርት"}'::jsonb, 'Allium cepa var. asculonicum Barker', 'DZARC', 'http://196.191.93.34/moa-portal/cropopen/varieites/crops/shallot.jpg', 'Shallot (Allium cepa var. asculonicum Barker, syn. A. ascalonicum auct.non L.) is believed to have come from Western Asia. It is perennial and seldom produces seeds, but the bulb when planted divides into a number of cloves, which remain attached at the bottom.', 9, 'ACTIVE'),
  ('snap-bean', 'croptype-472025509543', 'fruit-and-vegetables', 'Snap bean', NULL, 'Phaseolus vulgaris L.', 'MARC', 'http://196.191.93.34/moa-portal/cropopen/varieites/crops/snapbean.jpg', NULL, 3, 'ACTIVE'),
  ('snap-pea', 'croptype-057528874289', 'fruit-and-vegetables', 'Snap pea', NULL, 'Pisum satium var. macrocarpon', NULL, 'http://196.191.93.34/moa-portal/cropopen/varieites/crops/snapPea.jpg', NULL, 2, 'ACTIVE'),
  ('snow-pea', 'croptype-498660153925', 'fruit-and-vegetables', 'Snow pea', NULL, 'Pisum sativum var. saccharatum', 'HARC', 'http://196.191.93.34/moa-portal/cropopen/varieites/crops/snowpea.jpg', NULL, 2, 'ACTIVE'),
  ('sorghum', 'croptype-520366975124', 'cereal', 'Sorghum', '{"am": "ማሽላ"}'::jsonb, 'Sorghum bicolar', 'MARC', 'http://196.191.93.34/moa-portal/cropopen/varieites/crops/sorghum.jpg', 'Sorthum is one of the major crops produced in Ethiopia, and it is the fourth important crop in terms of area coverage and volume of prouction. It is adapted to a wide range of environment, and henve can be producted in the high lands, medium altitude and low land areas. It is widely produced more than any other crops, in thee areas where there is moisture stress. In 2020/21 cropping season, sorhum is produced on about 1,6679,277.06 ha of land from which 45,173,502.18 quintals of yield are obtained', 66, 'ACTIVE'),
  ('soybean', 'croptype-551595836628', 'oil-seeds', 'Soybean', '{"am": "አኩሪ አተር"}'::jsonb, 'Glycine max', 'JARC', 'http://196.191.93.34/moa-portal/cropopen/varieites/crops/soybean.jpg', 'Soybean is an internationally known important pulse crop. It is used for different purposes. In the 2020/21 cropping season, this crop covers about 83,797.17 hectares of land with an estimated production not less than 2,086,763.89 quintals. Since the oil content is high (16% and above) it is used for edible oil production. The by-product is cheap and an important source of protein for both human consumption & animal feed. It can also be used as Soya milk and Soya meat.', 36, 'ACTIVE'),
  ('spanish-mint', 'croptype-536373285121', 'spices-condiments-medicinal-aromatic', 'Spanish mint', '{"am": "ናና"}'::jsonb, 'Mentha spicata ''Spanish pointed''', 'WGARC', 'http://196.191.93.34/moa-portal/cropopen/varieites/crops/Spanish mint.jpg', NULL, 1, 'ACTIVE'),
  ('spearmint', 'croptype-670738359780', 'spices-condiments-medicinal-aromatic', 'Spearmint', '{"am": "ናና"}'::jsonb, 'Mentha spicata L.', 'WGARC', 'http://196.191.93.34/moa-portal/cropopen/varieites/crops/Spearmint.jpg', NULL, 2, 'ACTIVE'),
  ('stevia', 'croptype-310780138063', 'spices-condiments-medicinal-aromatic', 'Stevia', '{"am": "ስቴቪያ"}'::jsonb, 'Stevia rebaudiana Bertoni L.', 'WGARC', 'http://196.191.93.34/moa-portal/cropopen/varieites/crops/stevia.webp', NULL, 1, 'ACTIVE'),
  ('sugarcane', 'croptype-926200460059', 'industrial-crops', 'Sugarcane', '{"am": "ሸንኮራ"}'::jsonb, 'Saccharum officinarum', 'Sugar Corporation', 'http://196.191.93.34/moa-portal/cropopen/varieites/crops/sugarcane.jpg', NULL, 4, 'ACTIVE'),
  ('summer-squash', 'croptype-017503164196', 'fruit-and-vegetables', 'Summer squash', NULL, 'Cucurbita pepo', 'MARC', 'http://196.191.93.34/moa-portal/cropopen/varieites/crops/summer-squash.jpg', NULL, 1, 'ACTIVE'),
  ('sunflower', 'croptype-671707385473', 'oil-seeds', 'Sunflower', '{"am": "ሱፍ"}'::jsonb, 'Helianthus annuus', 'HARC', 'http://196.191.93.34/moa-portal/cropopen/varieites/crops/Sunflower.jpg', 'Sunflower is native to the Central America. Sunflower oil is used for cooking, as carrier oil and to produce margarine and bio-deiseal. According to the Central Statistics The total area under production during 2020/21 was 4,150.55 hectares and the production was estimated to be over 42,878.01 quintals.', 18, 'ACTIVE'),
  ('sweet-annie', 'croptype-818791209390', 'spices-condiments-medicinal-aromatic', 'Sweet annie', '{"am": "አርተሚዚያ"}'::jsonb, 'Artemisia annua', 'WGARC', 'http://196.191.93.34/moa-portal/cropopen/varieites/crops/Sweet annie.jpg', NULL, 1, 'ACTIVE'),
  ('sweet-corn', 'croptype-761550815879', 'fruit-and-vegetables', 'Sweet corn', NULL, 'Zea mays var. rugosa', NULL, 'http://196.191.93.34/moa-portal/cropopen/varieites/crops/sweetCorn.jpg', NULL, 1, 'ACTIVE'),
  ('sweet-potato', 'croptype-310332039024', 'roots-and-tubers', 'Sweet potato', '{"am": "ስኳር ድንች"}'::jsonb, 'Ipomoea batatas', 'HawARC', 'http://196.191.93.34/moa-portal/cropopen/varieites/crops/sweet_potato.jpg', 'Sweet potato is a dicotyledonous plant that belongs to the family Convolvulaceae. Its large, starchy, sweet tasting tuberous roots are an important root vegetable. The young leaves and shoots are sometimes eaten as greens. It is one of the major root crops of Ethiopia, which is cultivated around hoe for several years and is used for food and feed. Sweet potato is mostly cultivated in the south, southwest and east of the county.', 29, 'ACTIVE'),
  ('taro', 'croptype-898168031958', 'roots-and-tubers', 'Taro', NULL, 'Colocasia esculenta', 'JARC', 'http://196.191.93.34/moa-portal/cropopen/varieites/crops/taro.jpg', 'Taro is known as Godere in Ethiopia. The part eaten is the corm which is formed underwound by the thickening of the base of the stem. The crop is propagated by cutting from the top part of the corm or by planting cormels.', 3, 'ACTIVE'),
  ('tef', 'croptype-920196427806', 'cereal', 'Tef', '{"am": "ጤፍ"}'::jsonb, 'Eragrostis tef', 'DZARC', 'http://196.191.93.34/moa-portal/cropopen/varieites/crops/Tef.jpg', 'Tef is a gluten-free an important cereal crop in Ethiopia. In 2020/21 cropping season, cereal crops were grown on 10,538,341.91 hectares of land. Of these, 2,928,206.26 hectares were allocated for Tef and the total production in the Meher season was about 55,099,615.14 quintals.

Outside Ethiopia there is a growing interest in using tef. For example, small scale commercial production of tef has begun in a few areas of the wheat belts of USA, Canada and Australia. Tef has been introduced to South Africa and cultivated as a forage crop, and in recent years cultivated as a cereal crop in Northern Kenya and The Netherlands.

Tef is endemic to Ethiopia and its major diversity is found only in that county. As with several other crops, the exact date and location for the domestication of Tef is unknown. However, there is not doubt that it is a very ancient crop in Ethiopia, where domestication took place before the birth of Christ.

In Ethiopia, tef is traditionally grown as a cereal crop. The grain is ground to flour, which is mainly used for making popular pancake-like local bread called enjera and sometimes for making porridge. The grain is also used to make local alcoholic drinks, called tela and katikala. Tef starw, besides being the most appreciated feed for cattle, is also used to reinforce mud and plaster the walls of tukuls and local grain storage facilities called goteras. Tef grain, owing to its high mineral content, has started to be used in mixtures with soybean, chickpea and other grains in the baby food industry. It is the most adapted crop in the diverse agro-ecologies of the country.', 58, 'ACTIVE'),
  ('tobaco', 'croptype-833789386136', 'industrial-crops', 'Tobaco', '{"am": "ትምባሆ"}'::jsonb, 'Nicotiana tabacum', 'National Tobaco Enterprise', 'http://196.191.93.34/moa-portal/cropopen/varieites/crops/tobaco.jpg', NULL, 2, 'ACTIVE'),
  ('tomato', 'croptype-322963603333', 'fruit-and-vegetables', 'Tomato', '{"am": "ቲማቲም"}'::jsonb, 'Lycopersicum esculentum. Mill', 'MARC', 'http://196.191.93.34/moa-portal/cropopen/varieites/crops/tomato.jpg', NULL, 56, 'ACTIVE'),
  ('triticale', 'croptype-554879135329', 'cereal', 'Triticale', NULL, 'X-Triticosecale', 'AdARC', 'http://196.191.93.34/moa-portal/cropopen/varieites/crops/triticale.webp', 'Triticale (X. Triticosecale) is a man-made crop developed by crossing wheat (Triticum turgidum or Triticum aestivum) with Rye (Secale cereale). In Ethiopia, triticale is a recent introduction. Triticale can be cultivated in a wide range of agro-ecologies, ranging from sea level to over 3000 m.a.s.l. Drought and frost tolerance are the primary advantages that triticale has over other cereal crops. It also exhibits better performance under acidic and degraded soils compared with many other cereals. Triticale has high biomass production and re-growth capacity for grazing. The yield advantage over wheat and barley is also significant.

Triticale is adapted to a wide range of soil conditions ranging from sandy to clay soil types. It requires an average of 500-600 mm rainfall, well distributed during the growing season. However, it can also perform well with as little as 350 mm of seasonal rainfall.

Most cultural practices for growing wheat can be applied directedly to triticale. Consequently, the fertilization, seedbed preparation, seeding depth and seeding methods used for wheat are acceptable for triticale. Triticale can be used for making enjera, pasta, pastry, bread, tella and beer. Triticale bread and enjera products have been well accepted by farmers in South Gondar.', 10, 'ACTIVE'),
  ('turmeric', 'croptype-660038989844', 'spices-condiments-medicinal-aromatic', 'Turmeric', '{"am": "እርድ"}'::jsonb, 'Curcuma domestica', 'TNSRC', 'http://196.191.93.34/moa-portal/cropopen/varieites/crops/turmeric.webp', NULL, 2, 'ACTIVE'),
  ('vanilla', 'croptype-649571398221', 'spices-condiments-medicinal-aromatic', 'Vanilla', '{"am": "ቫኒላ"}'::jsonb, 'Vanilla planifolia', 'TNSRC', 'http://196.191.93.34/moa-portal/cropopen/varieites/crops/Vanilla.jpg', NULL, 1, 'ACTIVE'),
  ('vernonia', 'croptype-251112141583', 'industrial-crops', 'Vernonia', NULL, 'Vernonia galamensis', 'WGARC', 'http://196.191.93.34/moa-portal/cropopen/varieites/crops/vernonia.webp', 'Vernonia galamensis is industrial crop with very high content of vernolic acid in the seed oil. The products that can be made from vernonia include epoxies for manufacturing adhesives, varnishes and paints, and industrial coatings. The low viscosity of Vernonial oil would allow it to be used as a non-volatile solvent in oil based-paints since it will become incorporated in the dry paint rather than evaporating in to the air, which reduces pollution.', 1, 'ACTIVE'),
  ('water-melon', 'croptype-531562263904', 'fruit-and-vegetables', 'Water melon', '{"am": "ሐባብ"}'::jsonb, 'Citrullus lanatus', 'MARC', 'http://196.191.93.34/moa-portal/cropopen/varieites/crops/waterMelon.jpg', NULL, 10, 'ACTIVE'),
  ('white-cumin', 'croptype-928350012475', 'spices-condiments-medicinal-aromatic', 'White cumin', '{"am": "ነጭ አዝሙድ"}'::jsonb, 'Nigella sativa (white cumin)', 'GoARC', 'http://196.191.93.34/moa-portal/cropopen/varieites/crops/whiteCumin.webp', NULL, 2, 'ACTIVE'),
  ('wine-grape', 'croptype-568102620935', 'fruit-and-vegetables', 'Wine grape', '{"am": "ወይን"}'::jsonb, 'Vitis vinifera', 'DZARC', 'http://196.191.93.34/moa-portal/cropopen/varieites/crops/Wine grape.jpg', 'Ethiopian grape wine represents a growing and promising segment of the country’s agricultural and agro-processing sector. Produced mainly from grapes cultivated in highland and Rift Valley areas, Ethiopian grape wine reflects the country’s diverse agro-ecological conditions, characterized by abundant sunshine, moderate temperatures, and suitable altitudes that favor grape quality and sugar accumulation. The wine industry in Ethiopia combines traditional agricultural practices with modern viticulture and winemaking technologies. Locally produced wines are typically made from both introduced and adapted grape varieties, resulting in wines that range from light and fruity to fuller-bodied styles. Ethiopian grape wines often exhibit fresh acidity, mild tannins, and pleasant aromas, making them suitable for local consumption and emerging regional markets. Beyond its beverage value, grape wine production contributes to employment creation, value addition, and income diversification for farmers and agro-industries. The sector also supports the development of associated industries such as glass manufacturing, packaging, and tourism. With continued investment in improved varieties, vineyard management, and quality control, Ethiopian grape wine has strong potential to enhance domestic supply and gradually compete in international niche markets. Overall, Ethiopian grape wine symbolizes the country’s evolving capacity to transform agricultural produce into high-value products while promoting agro-industrial development and economic growth.', 11, 'ACTIVE'),
  ('yam', 'croptype-914145610558', 'roots-and-tubers', 'Yam', NULL, 'Dioscorea spp', 'HawARC', 'http://196.191.93.34/moa-portal/cropopen/varieites/crops/yam.jpg', NULL, 5, 'ACTIVE'),
  ('yellow-courgette', 'croptype-112866462069', 'fruit-and-vegetables', 'Yellow courgette', NULL, 'Cucurbita spp', NULL, 'http://196.191.93.34/moa-portal/cropopen/varieites/crops/yellowcourage.jpg', NULL, 1, 'ACTIVE'),
  ('ziziphus-kurkura', 'croptype-149942674759', 'fruit-and-vegetables', 'Ziziphus (Kurkura)', '{"am": "ኩርኩራ"}'::jsonb, 'Ziziphus jujuba', 'MARC', 'http://196.191.93.34/moa-portal/cropopen/varieites/crops/ziziphus.jfif', NULL, 2, 'ACTIVE');

